From 9145afb52539f32d3c03ee6b3694e656613a845c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RDoom <171243930+aeon1911@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:51:30 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 41/49] Switch: no SD stalls through the zip mutex, rare list
 saves, stabilizer on

HW test of 5625345a5: explosions and doors smooth; a 57 ms BeginFrame stall
was the texture list save (FString built line by line), a 2.4 s frame came
while the card was busy writing, and smoke fights still had half the frames
late with the GPU fill-bound at 60% resolution.

- FZipFile::SetEntryAddress reads the local header without holding the
  mutex (a thread waiting for the SD card blocked every thread opening a new
  entry, the renderer included); release/acquire fences between the new
  position and the cleared flag, which readers check without the mutex.
- Texture list: built in a reserved std::string; first save one second
  after the first new picture of a session, then at most every 20 s.
- nx_stabilizer 60 by default on the Switch: purely visual detail (faint
  and distant effects, lights, shadows) is trimmed only while frames are late.
- Frames held back by the tic rate (menu, pause) count neither for the
  stabilizer nor for the dynamic resolution.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
